nal Group, Inc. was founded in 2002 and is headquartered in Temple, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ramey Pierce Jackson | CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $550K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $71K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Janus International Group, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $467M market cap on $884M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 39%.","The business throws off $114M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.59\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 5.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"News sentiment running negative (-0.14) across recent coverage","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 78% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 45% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Janus (NYSE: JBI) swings to a Q3 loss as adjusted EBITDA slides","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/janus-nyse-jbi-swings-to-a-q3-loss-as-adjusted-ebitda-slides.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794528905.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Janus International Group (NYSE:JBI) Shares Down 4.2% on Disappointing Earnings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/janus-international-group-nysejbi-shares-down-4-2-on-disappointing-earnings.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794414061.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"JBI Q3 2026 deep dive: management cuts guidance amid self-storage market headwinds","source":"stockstory.org","link":"h